From 8eeaee24651d8002011387350b6bb08cf629306f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:16:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/71] video: rockchip: rga3: release session buffers by
 reference on close

When a client closes /dev/rga, rga_mm_session_release_buffer() walked the
memory_idr and called rga_mm_force_releaser_buffer() on every buffer owned
by the session. That helper unconditionally idr_remove()s, unmaps and
kfree()s the buffer, ignoring its kref refcount.

Buffer imports are de-duplicated across the whole memory_idr
(rga_mm_lookup_external() has no per-session filter) and internal_buffer->
session records only the first importer, so a second session that imports
the same dma-buf/address shares the handle and holds a reference. A running
job also takes a reference in rga_mm_get_buffer(). Force-freeing on close
therefore frees memory that another session or an in-flight job still
references, leaving a dangling pointer; a later put or use can then fault
on the freed object at a random address.

Drop only the exiting session's reference through the normal
kref_put(&buffer->refcount, rga_mm_kref_release_buffer) path, so the buffer
is unmapped and freed only when the last reference goes away. When a
reference survives, detach ->session (the owner is gone) so nothing later
dereferences the freed session or misattributes a reused session address,
and log the leftover refcount to pinpoint the stage if it recurs.

rga_mm_force_releaser_buffer() is still used by the driver-remove path
(rga_mm_buffer_destroy_for_idr()), where all sessions are already gone.

Signed-off-by: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_mm.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_mm.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_mm.c
index 3d54c39b026e8..33825e1dc9e46 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_mm.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga3/rga_mm.c
@@ -2845,11 +2845,36 @@ int rga_mm_session_release_buffer(struct rga_session *session)
 	mutex_lock(&mm->lock);
 
 	idr_for_each_entry(&mm->memory_idr, buffer, i) {
-		if (session == buffer->session) {
+		if (session != buffer->session)
+			continue;
+
+		/*
+		 * Imports are de-duplicated across the whole memory_idr
+		 * (rga_mm_lookup_external() has no session filter), and a
+		 * running job also holds a reference (rga_mm_get_buffer()).
+		 * So a buffer owned by the exiting session may still be
+		 * referenced elsewhere. Drop only this session's reference
+		 * through the normal kref path instead of forcibly unmapping
+		 * and freeing, so a surviving reference is never left pointing
+		 * at freed memory.
+		 */
+		if (kref_read(&buffer->refcount) > 1) {
+			rga_err("[tgid:%d] handle[%d] still referenced at exit (refcount=%u), dropping session reference only\n",
+			       session->tgid, buffer->handle,
+			       kref_read(&buffer->refcount));
+			/*
+			 * The session is going away; detach it so the surviving
+			 * reference does not dereference the freed session and a
+			 * future session reusing this address is not mistaken
+			 * for the owner here.
+			 */
+			buffer->session = NULL;
+		} else {
 			rga_err("[tgid:%d] Destroy handle[%d] when the user exits\n",
 			       session->tgid, buffer->handle);
-			rga_mm_force_releaser_buffer(buffer);
 		}
+
+		kref_put(&buffer->refcount, rga_mm_kref_release_buffer);
 	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&mm->lock);
